#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:1
msgid "llc - LLVM static compiler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:8
msgid "{program}`llc` \\[*options*\\] \\[*filename*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:12
msgid ""
"The {program}`llc` command compiles LLVM source inputs into assembly "
"language for a specified architecture. The assembly language output can then "
"be passed through a native assembler and linker to generate a native "
"executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:16
msgid ""
"The choice of architecture for the output assembly code is automatically "
"determined from the input file, unless the {option}`-march` option is used "
"to override the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:20
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:22
msgid ""
"If `filename` is \"`-`\" or omitted, {program}`llc` reads from standard "
"input. Otherwise, it will read from `filename`. Inputs can be in either the "
"LLVM assembly language format (`.ll`) or the LLVM bitcode format (`.bc`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:26
msgid ""
"If the {option}`-o` option is omitted, then {program}`llc` will send its "
"output to standard output if the input is from standard input. If the "
"{option}`-o` option specifies \"`-`\", then the output will also be sent to "
"standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:30
msgid ""
"If no {option}`-o` option is specified and an input file other than \"`-`\" "
"is specified, then {program}`llc` creates the output filename by taking the "
"input filename, removing any existing `.bc` extension, and adding a `.s` "
"suffix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:34
msgid "Other {program}`llc` options are described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:36
msgid "End-user Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:39
msgid "Print a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:43
msgid ""
"Pass target-specific InstPrinter options. Refer to the `-M` option of "
"{manpage}`llvm-objdump(1)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:48
msgid ""
"Use `<filename>` as the output filename. See the summary above for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:53
msgid ""
"Generate code at different optimization levels. These correspond to the `-"
"O0`, `-O1`, `-O2`, and `-O3` optimization levels used by {program}`clang`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:59
msgid ""
"Override the target triple specified in the input file with the specified "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:64
msgid ""
"Specify the architecture for which to generate assembly, overriding the "
"target encoded in the input file. See the output of `llc -help` for a list "
"of valid architectures. By default this is inferred from the target triple "
"or autodetected to the current architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:71
msgid ""
"Specify a specific chip in the current architecture to generate code for. By "
"default this is inferred from the target triple and autodetected to the "
"current architecture. For a list of available CPUs, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:81
msgid ""
"Specify a specific chip microarchitecture in the current architecture to "
"tune code for. By default this is inferred from the target triple and "
"autodetected to the current architecture. For a list of available tuning "
"CPUs, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:92
msgid ""
"Specify what kind of output `llc` should generated. Options are: `asm` for "
"textual assembly ( `'.s'`), `obj` for native object files (`'.o'`) and "
"`null` for not emitting anything (for performance testing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:96
msgid "Note that not all targets support all options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:100
msgid ""
"Override or control specific attributes of the target, such as whether SIMD "
"operations are enabled or not. The default set of attributes is set by the "
"current CPU. For a list of available attributes, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:110
msgid ""
"Specify effect of frame pointer elimination optimization (all,non-leaf,none)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:114
msgid ""
"Disable optimizations that may produce excess precision for floating point. "
"Note that this option can dramatically slow down code on some systems (e.g. "
"X86)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:120
msgid "Enable optimizations that assume no Inf values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:124
msgid "Enable optimizations that assume no NAN values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:128
msgid ""
"Enable FP math optimizations that assume the sign of 0 is insignificant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:132
msgid "Print statistics recorded by code-generation passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:136
msgid ""
"Save LLVM statistics to a file in the current directory ({option}`--save-"
"stats`/\"--save-stats=cwd\") or the directory of the output file (\"--save-"
"stats=obj\") in JSON format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:142
msgid ""
"Record the amount of time needed for each pass and print a report to "
"standard error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:147
msgid ""
"Specify which EABI version should conform to. Valid EABI versions are *gnu*, "
"*4* and *5*. Default value (*default*) depends on the triple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:152
msgid ""
"Emit the .stack_sizes section which contains stack size metadata. The "
"section contains an array of pairs of function symbol values (pointer size) "
"and stack sizes (unsigned LEB128). The stack size values only include the "
"space allocated in the function prologue. Functions with dynamic stack "
"allocations are not included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:160
msgid ""
"Emit the \\_\\_remarks (MachO) section which contains metadata about remark "
"diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:164
msgid "Tuning/Configuration Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:167
msgid ""
"Print generated machine code after instruction selection (useful for "
"debugging)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:171
msgid "Specify the register allocator to use. Valid register allocators are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:174
msgid "*basic*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:175
msgid "Basic register allocator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:177
msgid "*fast*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:178
msgid "Fast register allocator. It is the default for unoptimized code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:180
msgid "*greedy*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:181
msgid "Greedy register allocator. It is the default for optimized code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:183
msgid "*pbqp*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:184
msgid ""
"Register allocator based on 'Partitioned Boolean Quadratic Programming'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:188
msgid ""
"Specify the spiller to use for register allocators that support it. "
"Currently this option is used only by the linear scan register allocator. "
"The default `spiller` is *local*. Valid spillers are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:192
msgid "*simple*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:193
msgid "Simple spiller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:195
msgid "*local*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:196
msgid "Local spiller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:199
msgid "Intel IA-32-specific Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:202
msgid ""
"Specify whether to emit assembly code in AT&T syntax (the default) or Intel "
"syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:206
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:208
msgid ""
"If {program}`llc` succeeds, it will exit with 0. Otherwise, if an error "
"occurs, it will exit with a non-zero value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:211
msgid "SEE ALSO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llc.md:213
msgid "{manpage}`lli(1)`"
msgstr ""
